Authfy - Enterprise API Management SaaS

Authfy is a developer-focused Identity & Access Management (IAM) platform. It allows users to generate, manage, and revoke secure API keys for their applications, similar to Stripe or OpenAI.

Architecture: Full-Stack Microservices (Dockerized)

🚀 Tech Stack

Backend: Java 21, Spring Boot 3, Spring Security 6, JPA/Hibernate

Frontend: React.js, Vite, Tailwind CSS

Database: MySQL 8.0

DevOps: Docker, Docker Compose, Nginx, Multi-Stage Builds

Security: BCrypt Hashing, SHA-256 API Key Hashing, JWT Authentication

🛠️ How to Run (The "One-Command" Deploy)

Prerequisites: Docker Desktop installed.

Clone the repository

git clone [https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/Authfy-Dockerized-SaaS.git](https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/Authfy-Dockerized-SaaS.git)
cd Authfy-Dockerized-SaaS


Start the Infrastructure
Run this single command to build and start Backend, Frontend, and Network:

docker-compose up --build


Access the App

Frontend: http://localhost:3000

Backend API: http://localhost:8080

